; A `let` binding a primitive is not representable in the term/proof encoding,
; so this file must be reported as not supporting proofs.
;
; The binding that matters is the second one. Global removal keeps the first
; one's expansion — including the declaration of the shared table both of them
; write to — inside the `fail`, so a check that only looks at the top level
; never learns the table is one, and stops recognizing the second binding as a
; global one at all.
(datatype Math (Num i64))

(fail (let $bad (/ 1 0)))

(let $limit 5)

(Num 1)
(check (Num 1))
